{"schema_version":"1.7.3","id":"GHSA-v2wj-7wpq-c8vv","published":"2026-03-03T18:31:33Z","modified":"2026-03-04T21:02:19.351838Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-0540"],"summary":"DOMPurify contains a Cross-site Scripting vulnerability","details":"DOMPurify 3.1.3 through 3.3.1 and 2.5.3 through 2.5.8, fixed in commit 729097f, contain a cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows attackers to bypass attribute sanitization by exploiting five missing rawtext elements (noscript, xmp, noembed, noframes, iframe) in the SAFE_FOR_XML regex. Attackers can include payloads like </noscript><img src=x onerror=alert(1)> in attribute values to execute JavaScript when sanitized output is placed inside these unprotected rawtext contexts.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"dompurify","ecosystem":"npm","purl":"pkg:npm/dompurify"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"3.1.3"},{"last_affected":"3.3.1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/03/GHSA-v2wj-7wpq-c8vv/GHSA-v2wj-7wpq-c8vv.json"}},{"package":{"name":"dompurify","ecosystem":"npm","purl":"pkg:npm/dompurify"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"2.5.3"},{"last_affected":"2.5.8"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/03/GHSA-v2wj-7wpq-c8vv/GHSA-v2wj-7wpq-c8vv.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-0540"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify/commit/fca0a938b4261ddc9c0293a289935a9029c049f5"},{"type":"PACKAGE","url":"https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/dompurify-xss-via-missing-rawtext-elements-in-safe-for-xml"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/dompurify-xss-via-missing-rawtext-elements-in-safeforxml"}],"database_specific":{"cwe_ids":["CWE-79"],"github_reviewed":true,"github_reviewed_at":"2026-03-04T2